    "body": "That would be great. The easiest way to do so right now is for you to create a branch in your CSC fork based on the B-ext-merge branch (https://github.com/RISC-V-Certification-Steering-Committee/riscv-isa-manual/tree/B-ext-merge). Then you can create a PR on the CSC fork targeting the B-ext-merge (instead of main) and it will update this PR automatically when it is merged. We'll figure out a better system soon, but this will work until that's sorted out.",
